"""CCAO-F group 2: Domain 6 (Governance, Risk, and Responsible Use) and Domain 7 (Troubleshooting and Optimization).

Questions, lessons, games, case study and cheat sheet for the two categories; the flashcards
(f1063-f1127) are in data/ccao_b1.py.

Written against the Claude Certified Associate - Foundations exam guide (version 1.0,
effective July 2026; weights 15% for Domain 6 and 10% for Domain 7) and checked in October 2026
against Anthropic's Usage Policy (high-risk use case requirements, disclosure, deceptive content,
discrimination, responsibility for agents), the Anthropic Privacy Center (consumer and commercial
data use, retention, DPA, BAA, certifications), the Claude Help Center (connectors, Projects,
sharing, file creation and prompt-injection cautions, how Claude marks AI-generated content, usage
limit best practices, error messages and prompt troubleshooting tips) and Anthropic's AI Fluency
framework (Diligence). Governance items are phrased as principles so that they stay true as the
products and policy pages change; they avoid dated figures.
"""


def _mc(i, cat, question, options, correct, explanation, why=None):
    q = {'id': i, 'cat': cat, 'type': 'mc', 'question': question, 'options': options, 'correct': correct, 'explanation': explanation}
    if why:
        q['whyTested'] = why
    return q


def _ms(i, cat, question, options, correct, explanation, why=None):
    q = {'id': i, 'cat': cat, 'type': 'ms', 'question': question, 'options': options, 'correct': correct, 'explanation': explanation}
    if why:
        q['whyTested'] = why
    return q


def _tf(i, cat, question, answer, explanation, why=None):
    q = {'id': i, 'cat': cat, 'type': 'tf', 'question': question, 'answer': answer, 'explanation': explanation}
    if why:
        q['whyTested'] = why
    return q


